# 🏢 ENTERPRISE DATA ARCHITECTURE & SCOPING POLICY
enterprise_structure_scoping:
  enforcement_level: HARD_FAIL
  description: "All new schemas, UI components, and API routes must conform to Oracle-style enterprise boundaries in addition to standard multi-tenancy."

  fundamental_rule:
    - "Tenant ID (tenant_id) is the absolute supreme boundary. Cross-tenant access is STRICTLY FORBIDDEN at all layers."
    - "All enterprise elements (Ledgers, LEs, BUs, Inv Orgs, SetIDs) exist strictly WITHIN a single Tenant."

  scoping_requirements:
    general_ledger (GL):
      scope: "Ledger ID"
      description: "Applies to journals, balances, and financial reporting."
    human_resources_and_payroll (HR_HCM):
      scope: "Legal Entity ID"
      description: "Workers, assignments, payroll runs, and tax reporting belong to a Legal Entity (NOT PSU or Legal Employer)."
      schema_column: "ent_legal_entity_id"
    financial_subledgers (AP_AR_PO_OM):
      scope: "Business Unit ID (BU)"
      description: "Applies to AP Invoices, AR Receipts, Purchase Orders, Sales Orders, and Expenses. A BU processes transactions and posts to a Ledger."
      schema_column: "ent_business_unit_id"
    supply_chain_and_manufacturing (INV_WMS_MFG):
      scope: "Inventory Organization ID"
      description: "Applies to physical material, on-hand balances, warehouses, work orders, and quality plans."
      schema_column: "ent_inventory_org_id"
    master_data (MDM):
      scope: "Reference Data Set ID (SetID)"
      description: "Applies to shared data like Customers, Suppliers, and Global PIM items shared across BUs."
      schema_column: "ent_set_id"

  ai_development_rules:
    - "When generating Drizzle schemas for transactional data, ALWAYS include the appropriate scoping column (e.g., ent_business_unit_id)."
    - "When generating API routes, ALWAYS enforce both the tenantId AND the active organizational context (BU, LE, or Inv Org)."
    - "When generating UI tables or forms, ALWAYS assume global state provides the user's Active Context, and filter/submit data accordingly."

# 🎨 FRONTEND UI/UX STANDARDIZATION POLICY
frontend_ui_standardization_policy:
  enforcement_level: HARD_FAIL
  description: "All new React components, UI interactions, and SPA routing must strictly adhere to Shadcn design system paradigms. Raw DOM manipulation and legacy browser primitives are completely forbidden."

  core_layout_and_data_display:
    - "Pages must exclusively use `StandardPage`, `StandardDashboard`, or `AdminLayout` wrappers."
    - "Legacy `<table>` tags are FORBIDDEN. Use `InteractiveSpreadsheet`, `DataTable`, or Shadcn `<Table>`."
    - "Native `<form>` tags are FORBIDDEN. Use Shadcn `<Form>` wraps combined with Zod validation."
    - "Hardcoded status colors (e.g., `bg-green-600`) are FORBIDDEN. Use semantic `<StatusBadge status={...} />`."

  primitives_and_accessibility:
    - "Raw `<label>`, `<button>`, `<input>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>` HTML tags are FORBIDDEN. Always use exact Shadcn equivalent primitives (`<Label>`, `<Button>`, `<Input>`, etc.)."
    - "Spoofing interactivity via `div role=\"button\" onClick={...}` is FORBIDDEN. Use `<Button variant=\"ghost\">` or valid semantic ARIA mappings."
    - "Icon-only `<Button>` elements MUST contain explicitly defined `aria-label` properties."
    - "Custom `<svg>` sizing logic using `size={24}` on Lucide icons is FORBIDDEN. Use Tailwind semantic classes: `className=\"h-6 w-6\"`."
    - "External anchor tags `target=\"_blank\"` MUST have `rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`."

  state_routing_and_dialogs:
    - "Native `window.location.href='/path'` or `<a href=\"...\">` bindings for internal SPA paths are FORBIDDEN. Always utilize Wouter `<Link>` API to preserve local React state cache."
    - "Direct document queries for state like `document.getElementById('xyz').value` are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN. Use React `useState`, Ref bindings, or `react-hook-form` paradigms."
    - "Native `window.confirm()`, `window.alert()`, or `prompt()` dialogues are FORBIDDEN. Leverage `<AlertDialog>`, `<Dialog>`, or `<PromptDialog>` modules maintaining dark-mode UI consistency."
    - "Custom tab mechanisms built via raw `useState` and mapped `<divs>` are FORBIDDEN. Inherit the standardized Shadcn `<Tabs>` component hierarchy."

  styles_and_theming:
    - "React inline styles (`style={{ padding: '...' }}`) are FORBIDDEN. Rely purely on Tailwind class combinations to preserve Content Security Policies. E.g. `<div className=\"pt-2\">` instead of `<div style={{ paddingTop: '8px' }}>`."
    - "Arbitrary exact typographic measurements (`text-[10px]`) are FORBIDDEN. Stick purely to native generic utility variables (`text-xs`, `text-sm`)."
    - "Raw HEX strings passing Tailwind colors (`bg-[#ffffff]`, `border-gray-200`) are FORBIDDEN as they aggressively block dark-mode toggle hooks. Use generic semantic layout themes: `bg-card`, `border-border`, `text-muted-foreground`."
    - "Standalone manual CSS files (`.css`) are strictly FORBIDDEN to be imported locally except for global index loaders. Everything must compile into dynamic specific inline Tailwind mappings."
    - "Manual progress indicators built with inline `style={{ width: '45%' }}` strings are FORBIDDEN. Wrap Shadcn `<Progress value={45} />`."

  dashboard_cards_and_analytics:
    - "Stat block `<Card>` elements MUST use the `color` and `variant` props inside `<MetricCard>` instead of hard-coded inline Tailwind color utilities (`bg-green-50 text-green-700`)."
    - "Arbitrary `<div>` badges displaying Status text MUST use the `<StatusBadge>` component semantic."

  performance_and_render_cycles:
    - "All constant spreadsheet and table definition arrays MUST be wrapped natively in a `useMemo(() => [...], [])` hook to prevent rapid DOM tearing on re-renders."

  best_practices:
    - "`console.log` statements are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN in any committed code across `src/pages` or `src/components`. Code must be rigorously clean."
    - "Data components submitting requests (`<Button type=\"submit\">`) MUST bind to `disabled={form.formState.isSubmitting}`. Never allow multi-click accidental submits."
    - "Hard-coded locales (e.g. `en-US` or `USD`) are FORBIDDEN. Use `useTenantLocale()` and pass values correctly into `formatters.ts`."
